                                "text": "Придёт человек, наделённый всеми признаками Бога: вездесущий, всемогущий, всеведущий."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2738b4bf-fc60-46a0-ab7a-064487053f69",
                                "sense_id": "c2ac97b8-4961-38ad-ba03-8d40a6f102c8",
                                "text": "Только оторванные от своих полей, они оставались один на один с вездесущим верховным Богом."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9e9fe333-1520-387e-98c4-2ef590767938",
                        "entry_id": "56c7be28-5ab0-3f3e-9d2d-8857fc84bf99",
                        "glosses": [
                            "перен., шутл. во всём принимающий участие, всюду поспевающий"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "31279257-723d-4c85-8d62-65da3e37e8f0",
                                "sense_id": "9e9fe333-1520-387e-98c4-2ef590767938",
                                "text": "Громко было от мышей, вечно прожорливых, серых вездесущих тварей, что к холодам перекочевали из сада, где собрали весь урожай, в подпол и в простенки этого баракоподобного здания ― судьбоносного, однако, и для них."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3a030b9d-e229-4570-8cab-fcb705d7a896",
                                "sense_id": "9e9fe333-1520-387e-98c4-2ef590767938",
                                "text": "Мой вездесущий брат всё лето гонял на велосипеде по городу, умудряясь за день досадить и отцу с Лизой, и бабке с дедом, и всем, кому попадался на пути."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4ca3eaeb-6807-401e-aee1-9eea1804a886",
                        "source_entry_id": "56c7be28-5ab0-3f3e-9d2d-8857fc84bf99",
                        "target_lang_word": "omnipresent",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "omnipresent",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "73c15c30-da39-3794-8af0-2a51d0b15a47",
                                        "entry_id": "de82cc28-fa66-3e0c-aaa5-d4f23efc5ff9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Being everywhere simultaneously."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1bb95ef6-a39e-4798-9699-f662866974c8",
                                                "sense_id": "73c15c30-da39-3794-8af0-2a51d0b15a47",
                                                "text": "In 1975, China was emerging from the Cultural Revolution, its government’s effort to purify and revitalize society. Communist officials had set up indoctrination programs, broadcast propaganda over omnipresent loudspeakers, and sought to stamp out any evidence of China’s ancient history."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "202a6029-ac78-49f6-973b-1b2707519660",
                                                "sense_id": "73c15c30-da39-3794-8af0-2a51d0b15a47",
                                                "text": "Another most notable change concerns rolling stock liveries. Back then, corporate Rail Blue was omnipresent, whereas now there is a kaleidoscope of colours and styles."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9b0b57fd-495b-4800-9a28-c60b82ce188a",
                        "source_entry_id": "56c7be28-5ab0-3f3e-9d2d-8857fc84bf99",
                        "target_lang_word": "ubiquitous",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ubiquitous",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0e964613-b452-3006-b03e-85b348af8da5",
                                        "entry_id": "0b5237f7-dbd9-3199-8759-344579f92bec",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Being everywhere at once: omnipresent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "31a7d3da-edd7-4dc0-ab7c-110bfafa8060",
                                                "sense_id": "0e964613-b452-3006-b03e-85b348af8da5",
                                                "text": "In Christianity, Hinduism, and Judaism, God is ubiquitous."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "308be6e5-7be5-38eb-8f32-790a92312c03",
                                        "entry_id": "0b5237f7-dbd9-3199-8759-344579f92bec",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Appearing to be everywhere at once; being or seeming to be in more than one location at the same time."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "508734df-94dc-4189-a1f2-7337a00648e5",
                                                "sense_id": "308be6e5-7be5-38eb-8f32-790a92312c03",
                                                "text": "One of the wild suggestions referred to, as at last coming to be linked with the White Whale in the minds of the superstitiously inclined, was the unearthly conceit that Moby Dick was ubiquitous; that he had actually been encountered in opposite latitudes at one and the same instant of time."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "89d428c4-d987-44a4-aea3-33d4848613b4",
                                                "sense_id": "308be6e5-7be5-38eb-8f32-790a92312c03",
                                                "text": "There is much sad evidence, too, of the spoliation and dereliction of vanished industry: tips, slag-heaps and derelict colliery-screens among which the ubiquitous, nomad mountain sheep graze unconcernedly."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "332d3f22-d45b-43cb-9648-0cc9eca5c792",
                                                "sense_id": "308be6e5-7be5-38eb-8f32-790a92312c03",
                                                "text": "This deed accomplished, life no longer suffers hopelessly under the terrible mutilations of ubiquitous disaster, battered by time, hideous throughout space; but with its horror visible still, its cries of anguish still tumultuous, it becomes penetrated by an all-suffusing, all-sustaining love, and a knowledge of its own unconquered power."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bc2de8a9-ecd6-3d22-8c72-8c73a338bcfe",
                                        "entry_id": "0b5237f7-dbd9-3199-8759-344579f92bec",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Widespread; very prevalent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
